WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.670
Ananya asks her college placement bot a simple

2
00:00:02.705 --> 00:00:05.573
question: what is my CGPA?

3
00:00:05.923 --> 00:00:08.593
But a language model only writes text. It

4
00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:11.240
can't open the college database. Left alone, it

5
00:00:11.264 --> 00:00:12.471
would guess.

6
00:00:12.821 --> 00:00:15.097
So your app sends her question together with

7
00:00:15.131 --> 00:00:17.453
a menu of tools. Each tool has a

8
00:00:17.535 --> 00:00:20.948
name, a description, and the arguments it needs.

9
00:00:21.298 --> 00:00:23.759
The model never sees your Python code. Only

10
00:00:23.817 --> 00:00:24.874
this menu.

11
00:00:25.224 --> 00:00:27.558
The model doesn't answer. It replies with a

12
00:00:27.616 --> 00:00:30.681
tool call: the function name, get student, and

13
00:00:30.727 --> 00:00:32.840
the arguments as JSON.

14
00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:35.500
Notice what did not happen. Nothing has run

15
00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:37.741
yet. The model only asked.

16
00:00:38.091 --> 00:00:40.750
Your code parses the arguments, checks them, and

17
00:00:40.808 --> 00:00:44.082
runs the real Python function against the database.

18
00:00:44.432 --> 00:00:46.371
Because your code sits in the middle, a

19
00:00:46.441 --> 00:00:48.774
wrong roll number becomes a clear error, not

20
00:00:48.821 --> 00:00:49.912
a crash.

21
00:00:50.262 --> 00:00:52.387
Then it adds the result to the conversation

22
00:00:52.549 --> 00:00:54.674
as a tool message, and calls the model

23
00:00:54.743 --> 00:00:56.392
a second time.

24
00:00:56.742 --> 00:00:58.449
Now the model has the facts, so it

25
00:00:58.483 --> 00:01:01.316
writes the answer: your CGPA is eight point

26
00:01:01.386 --> 00:01:02.361
four.

27
00:01:02.711 --> 00:01:05.822
One question, two API calls. And the model

28
00:01:05.892 --> 00:01:08.098
chose that tool using only the description you

29
00:01:08.144 --> 00:01:09.259
wrote.

30
00:01:09.609 --> 00:01:12.628
So remember the split: the model proposes, your

31
00:01:12.697 --> 00:01:14.207
code executes.

32
00:01:14.557 --> 00:01:16.554
Next lesson: put this in a loop, and

33
00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:17.715
you have an agent.
